  "prefLabel": "Ins 3006.01 Protection of Fair Credit Reporting Act",
  "priorExpiration": "2009-07-01",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Ins 3006.01 Protection of Fair Credit Reporting Act. Nothing in this rule shall be construed to modify, limit, or supersede the operation of the federal Fair Credit Reporting Act (15 U.S.C. 1681 et seq.), and no inference shall be drawn on the basis of the provisions of this rule regarding whether information is transaction or experience information under Section 603 of that Act.\n\nSource. #7500, eff 7-1-01, EXPIRED: 7-1-09\n\nNew. #9922, eff 5-6-11; ss by #12749, eff 5-6-19",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/ins3000.html"
